{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-33454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(4,-2,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩=27.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩ & =27 \\\\ -3x+2y+3z & =27 \\\\ 3z & =27+3x-2y \\\\ z & =9+x-\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=6$ and $y=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=9+6-\\frac{2}{3}(3)=13.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(6,3,13)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,3,13⟩-⟨4,-2,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,5,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-3,2,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+10+18|}{\\sqrt{9+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|22|}{\\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d72988a0785a347d65bed5dd83fc7047617de8693215da214ff4b79eead2306"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\sqrt{11}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{22}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-33454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{22}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-34070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(2,1,3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $3x-6y-6z=-15.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-34070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=-1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-6y-6z & =-15 \\\\ 3(1)-6(-1)-6z & =-15 \\\\ -6z & =-24 \\\\ z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,-1,4)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-1,4⟩-⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨3,-6,-6⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-6)|}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-6)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-3+12-6|}{\\sqrt{9+36+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-34070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d72988a0785a347d65bed5dd83fc7047617de8693215da214ff4b79eead2306"} {"question" "q-34070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-34070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-34070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-80117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,4,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $6x-3y+6z=-18.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-80117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-3y+6z & =-18 \\\\ 6(1)-3(2)+6z & =-18 \\\\ 6z & =-18 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,2,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,2,-3⟩-⟨5,4,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨6,-3,6⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-24+6+6|}{\\sqrt{36+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,-12\\,|}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-80117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d72988a0785a347d65bed5dd83fc7047617de8693215da214ff4b79eead2306"} {"question" "q-80117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-80117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-80117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-129103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(3,-4,5)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,-4⟩=-42$, find the shortest distance from $P(1,-5,2)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-129103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-4,5⟩-⟨1,-5,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,-4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+4-12|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-129103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d72988a0785a347d65bed5dd83fc7047617de8693215da214ff4b79eead2306"} {"question" "q-129103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-129103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-129103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,5,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-4y+2z=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-4y+2z & =2 \\\\ 4(1)-4(1)+2z & =2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨-2,5,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-4,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12+16+8|}{\\sqrt{16+16+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d72988a0785a347d65bed5dd83fc7047617de8693215da214ff4b79eead2306"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5dacb"} {"question" "q-129163" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{17}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066317/state.json" "file_sha256" "d276924d0fd5bdabfd0f12dde1dc46d86640696a90ff5f201c839ebd41b5da